* Super-lead preamp, stage 2 of 4: the Overdrive channel (V2a, V2b). Node aa (after the 0.02u of V1b) arrives through VL1 into the Overdrive
* Volume network; V2b's plate and the mixing node's resistors are repeated at the output as its load (the Normal channel's branch as 2M2 to
* ground). See preamp.net for how the netlist is split.

.nodes x b3 aa bb ov g2a p2a k2a dd uu p2b k2b ww x1 g3b

V VRAIL x 701.9 378
R R62 x b3 15k
C C38 b3 0 10u

S VL1 aa 1 0
R R5 aa bb 470k
C C3 aa bb 2n
R VR_P1T bb ov 1
R VR_P1B ov 0 1
C C100 bb ov 1n
R R8 ov g2a 470k
